# Build output & generated
dist/
.astro/
node_modules/
build/

# Lockfile (npm owns its formatting)
package-lock.json

# Search index
public/pagefind/

# Content prose — leave authored Markdown/MDX untouched (Prettier reflows prose
# and can disturb KaTeX/MDX; formatting these offers little and risks churn).
src/content/

# Vendored / binary-ish
public/

# Agent tooling & design records — not site source.
.agents/
.claude/
.codex/
docs/

# Markdown everywhere: prose reflow is low-value and churny; keep hand-authored
# docs (README, AGENTS, DESIGN, asset READMEs) as written.
**/*.md
**/*.mdx

# .astro templates: prettier-plugin-astro reflows whitespace around inline
# elements, which CHANGES rendered output (e.g. adjacent <span>s in .pub-meta
# gain a stray space: "In preparation, 2026" -> "In preparation , 2026"). Verified
# against the built dist/. Formatting the .ts/.mjs/.css files is byte-safe; .astro
# is not, so we leave those hand-formatted. Editor Astro formatting is still fine
# per file — this only excludes them from the repo-wide `npm run format`.
**/*.astro
